# LeakShield Frozen Architecture

## Project

LeakShield is a 72-hour Zero Dependency Hackathon 2026 project.

It is a command-line repository security auditor written in Python 3.14.

Its purpose is to detect:

- leaked secrets and credentials
- suspicious credential-like values
- high-risk Python security patterns
- contextual security risks

It produces:

- CLI reports
- JSON reports
- HTML reports

## Absolute Dependency Constraint

LeakShield must contain ZERO external dependencies.

The implementation may import ONLY these approved modules:

argparse
pathlib
re
ast
json
html
hashlib
math
base64
fnmatch
os
unittest
datetime

Do NOT introduce any other imported module unless the architecture is explicitly changed and approved.

Do NOT:

- install pip packages
- use external APIs
- use cloud services
- call external security tools
- use subprocess
- vendor third-party libraries
- invoke package-installed CLI tools

Do not assume that another Python standard-library module is allowed merely because it is part of Python.

